  "term": "BST",
  "definition": "BST usually refers to the Block Span Task, a Corsi-block-like test of visuospatial working memory. In this source, it is described as an adapted version designed for use during MRI scanning to study visuospatial difficulties, including in people with Parkinson’s disease.",
